-- title:
--   Chart data on basic opens of the base-changed quotient tower
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $\mathcal O$ is a commutative domain which is a discrete valuation ring (`hdvr`), $\pi \in \mathcal O$ is irreducible (`hπ`), and $\mathcal O$ is $(\pi)$-adically complete (`hcomplete`); write $\mathcal O_n := \mathcal O/(\pi^{n+1})$.
--
--   **The tower $(X_n)$ and its group action.** Schemes $X_n$ are given together with morphisms $xb_n : X_n \to \operatorname{Spec} \mathcal O_n$ and $xt_n : X_n \to X_{n+1}$. The hypothesis `hcart` says that for each $n$ the square formed by $xt_n$, $xb_n$, $xb_{n+1}$ and $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the reduction $\mathcal O_{n+1} \to \mathcal O_n$ is a pullback; `hproper` and `hflat` say that every $xb_n$ is proper, resp. flat; `haff` says that every finite subset of $X_n$ is contained in an affine open. A finite group $G$ is given with homomorphisms $a_n : G \to \operatorname{Aut}(X_n)$ such that $xb_n \circ a_n(g) = xb_n$ (`ha_over`) and $q_{n+1}$-free compatibility with the transition maps, namely $a_{n+1}(g) \circ xt_n = xt_n \circ a_n(g)$ (`ha_xt`).
--
--   **The quotient datum.** $D$ is a `TowerQuotientDatum` for these data: it provides schemes $Y_n$ with morphisms $yb_n : Y_n \to \operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O_n$ and $yt_n : Y_n \to Y_{n+1}$ whose squares against the reductions $\mathcal O_{n+1}\to\mathcal O_n$ are pullbacks (`yt_isPullback`), each $yb_n$ being proper (`yb_isProper`) and flat (`yb_flat`), together with morphisms $p_n : X_n \to Y_n$ satisfying $yb_n \circ p_n = xb_n$ (`p_over`), $p_{n+1} \circ xt_n = yt_n \circ p_n$ (`p_xt`), the condition that the square $(xt_n, p_n, p_{n+1}, yt_n)$ be a pullback (`p_isPullback`), $G$-invariance $p_n \circ a_n(g) = p_n$ (`p_inv`), finiteness (`p_isFinite`) and surjectivity (`p_surjective`) of $p_n$, the condition that the restriction of $p_n$ over every open of $Y_n$ be an epimorphism (`p_epi_loc`), and a local universal property `univ_loc` which, for a scheme $T$, a family of opens $U_n \subseteq Y_n$ with $yt_n^{-1}U_{n+1} = U_n$ and morphisms $u_n : p_n^{-1}U_n \to T$ invariant under the restricted automorphisms $a_n(g)$, governs factorisation through the $U_n$.
--
--   **Flat base change.** $S$ is a commutative $\mathcal O$-algebra which is flat as an $\mathcal O$-module; write $\varpi$ for the image of $\pi$ in $S$ and $S_n := S/(\varpi^{n+1})$. Schemes $X'_n$ with morphisms $xb'_n : X'_n \to \operatorname{Spec} S_n$, $xt'_n : X'_n \to X'_{n+1}$, actions $a'_n : G \to \operatorname{Aut}(X'_n)$ and morphisms $q_n : X'_n \to X_n$ are given, subject to: `hq`, that $X'_n$ is the fibre product of $X_n$ and $\operatorname{Spec} S_n$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O_n$ (the square formed by $q_n$, $xb'_n$, $xb_n$ and $\operatorname{Spec}$ of $\mathcal O_n \to S_n$ is a pullback); `hcart'`, the analogue of `hcart` for the primed tower; `hq_xt`, $q_{n+1} \circ xt'_n = xt_n \circ q_n$; `hq_a`, $q_n \circ a'_n(g) = a_n(g) \circ q_n$; and `ha'_over`, $xb'_n \circ a'_n(g) = xb'_n$.
--
--   **Base change of the quotient tower.** Schemes $Y'_n$ with $yb'_n : Y'_n \to \operatorname{Spec} S_n$, $yt'_n : Y'_n \to Y'_{n+1}$, $p'_n : X'_n \to Y'_n$ and $r_n : Y'_n \to Y_n$ are given, subject to: `hbase`, that $Y'_n$ is the fibre product of $Y_n$ and $\operatorname{Spec} S_n$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O_n$; `hsq`, that the square $(q_n, p'_n, p_n, r_n)$ is a pullback, so $X'_n = X_n \times_{Y_n} Y'_n$; `hyt'r`, $r_{n+1} \circ yt'_n = yt_n \circ r_n$; `hyt'b`, compatibility of $yt'_n$ with $yb'_n$, $yb'_{n+1}$ and the reduction $S_{n+1} \to S_n$; `hp'_over`, $yb'_n \circ p'_n = xb'_n$; `hp'_inv`, $p'_n \circ a'_n(g) = p'_n$; and `hp'_xt`, $p'_{n+1} \circ xt'_n = yt'_n \circ p'_n$.
--
--   **Charts.** Opens $V_n \subseteq Y_n$ are given which are affine (`hVa`) and compatible, $yt_n^{-1}V_{n+1} = V_n$ (`hV`). A commutative ring $R$ is given, an $\mathcal O$-algebra carrying a multiplicative semiring action of $G$ commuting with the $\mathcal O$-action, such that $R$ is adically complete for the ideal generated by the image of $\pi$ (`hRc`), that image is a non-zero-divisor on $R$ (`hRtf`), and $R/\pi R$ is of finite type over $\mathcal O$ (`hRft`). Write $A := R^G$ for the fixed-point subalgebra `FixedPoints.subalgebra 𝒪 R G`. Ring isomorphisms $\mathrm{lvl}_n : R/(\pi^{n+1}) \xrightarrow{\ \sim\ } \Gamma(X_n, p_n^{-1}V_n)$ and $\mu_n : A/(\pi^{n+1}) \xrightarrow{\ \sim\ } \Gamma(Y_n, V_n)$ are given, subject to five compatibilities: `hlvl_xt`, the restriction map induced by $xt_n$ carries $\mathrm{lvl}_{n+1}(\bar x)$ to $\mathrm{lvl}_n(\bar x)$ for $x \in R$; `hlvl_smul`, the self-map of $\Gamma(X_n, p_n^{-1}V_n)$ induced by $a_n(g^{-1})$ carries $\mathrm{lvl}_n(\bar x)$ to $\mathrm{lvl}_n(\overline{g \cdot x})$; `hlvl_xb`, for $o \in \mathcal O$ the section $\mathrm{lvl}_n(\overline{o \cdot 1})$ is the image of $\bar o \in \mathcal O_n$ under $xb_n^{*}$ followed by restriction to $p_n^{-1}V_n$ (using the canonical isomorphism $\Gamma(\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O_n) \cong \mathcal O_n$); `hμ_yt`, the restriction map induced by $yt_n$ carries $\mu_{n+1}(\bar x)$ to $\mu_n(\bar x)$ for $x \in A$; `hμ_p`, the map $p_n^{*} : \Gamma(Y_n, V_n) \to \Gamma(X_n, p_n^{-1}V_n)$ carries $\mu_n(\bar x)$ to $\mathrm{lvl}_n$ of the class of $x$ viewed in $R$; and `hμ_yb`, the analogue of `hlvl_xb` for $\mu_n$ and $yb_n$. Finally, an element $b \in A \otimes_{\mathcal O} S$ is given.
--
--   **Conclusion.** There exist additive maps $\varphi_n : A \otimes_{\mathcal O} S \to \Gamma(Y'_n, r_n^{-1}V_n)$ such that:
--
--   (i) for all $n$, $x \in A$, $s \in S$, $\varphi_n(x \otimes s)$ is the product of the image of $\mu_n(\bar x)$ under $r_n^{*} : \Gamma(Y_n, V_n) \to \Gamma(Y'_n, r_n^{-1}V_n)$ with the image of $\bar s \in S_n$ under $yb'^{*}_n$ restricted to $r_n^{-1}V_n$;
--
--   (ii) every $\varphi_n$ is surjective;
--
--   (iii) the basic opens cut out by the chosen $b$ form a compatible family: there is a proof `hV'` that $yt'^{-1}_n\bigl(D(\varphi_{n+1}(b))\bigr) = D(\varphi_n(b))$ for all $n$, where $D(\cdot)$ denotes the basic open of a section of the structure sheaf; and, under this identification,
--
--   (iv) there exist a commutative ring $R'$, an $S$-algebra structure on it, a multiplicative semiring action of $G$ on $R'$ commuting with the $S$-action, such that $R'$ is adically complete for the ideal generated by the image of $\varpi$ in $R'$, that image is a non-zero-divisor on $R'$ (i.e. $\varpi x = 0$ implies $x = 0$), and the fixed-point subalgebra $R'^{G} =$ `FixedPoints.subalgebra S R' G` is likewise adically complete for the ideal generated by the image of $\varpi$; together with ring isomorphisms
--   $$\mathrm{lvl}'_n : R'/(\varpi^{n+1}) \xrightarrow{\ \sim\ } \Gamma\bigl(X'_n, p'^{-1}_n D(\varphi_n(b))\bigr), \qquad \mu'_n : R'^{G}/(\varpi^{n+1}) \xrightarrow{\ \sim\ } \Gamma\bigl(Y'_n, D(\varphi_n(b))\bigr)$$
--   satisfying the six compatibilities corresponding to those assumed for $\mathrm{lvl}_n$ and $\mu_n$: the restriction induced by $xt'_n$ carries $\mathrm{lvl}'_{n+1}(\bar x)$ to $\mathrm{lvl}'_n(\bar x)$ for $x \in R'$; the self-map induced by $a'_n(g^{-1})$ carries $\mathrm{lvl}'_n(\bar x)$ to $\mathrm{lvl}'_n(\overline{g \cdot x})$; for $s \in S$, $\mathrm{lvl}'_n$ of the class of the image of $s$ in $R'$ is the image of $\bar s \in S_n$ under $xb'^{*}_n$ restricted to $p'^{-1}_n D(\varphi_n(b))$; the restriction induced by $yt'_n$ carries $\mu'_{n+1}(\bar x)$ to $\mu'_n(\bar x)$ for $x \in R'^{G}$; the map $p'^{*}_n$ carries $\mu'_n(\bar x)$ to $\mathrm{lvl}'_n$ of the class of $x$ viewed in $R'$; and for $s \in S$, $\mu'_n$ of the class of the image of $s$ in $R'^{G}$ is the image of $\bar s \in S_n$ under $yb'^{*}_n$ restricted to $D(\varphi_n(b))$.
--
--   This is the chart-level input for flat base change of a tower quotient datum: over a cofinal system of affine opens of the base-changed quotient tower — the basic opens inside the pulled-back charts $r_n^{-1}V_n$, cut out by elements of the uncompleted tensor product $R^G \otimes_{\mathcal O} S$ — it produces the invariant-theoretic chart package ($\varpi$-adically complete, $\varpi$-torsion-free $S$-algebra with $G$-action, identifications of its truncations with sections upstairs and of its invariants with sections downstairs) in the same shape as the data assumed over $\mathcal O$. It is used in the proof of the local universal property for the base-changed datum, [`AlgebraicGeometry.TowerQuotientDatum.univ_loc_of_isPullback_of_flat`](thm.html#AlgebraicGeometry.TowerQuotientDatum.univ_loc_of_isPullback_of_flat), where such chart packages are glued.
